:Namespace Pipeline
⍝ Stream processing in APL: read orders from Kafka, keep running totals per
⍝ region, publish a summary after every batch.
⍝
⍝   orders  ──►  [ APL: totals per region (⌸) ]  ──►  order-stats
⍝
⍝ Restart-safe: on start it restores the last summary from order-stats, and
⍝ Kafka remembers how far the "apl-processor" group has read, so only new
⍝ orders are processed. Nothing is counted twice.
⍝
⍝ Live (prints as batches arrive):  kafka.sh processor   (LOAD= this file → Run)
⍝ Until idle, then exit:            kafka.sh run demo/process.apls

    ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1

    ∇ Load;home
    ⍝ Load Kafka.apln and Orders.apln into #
      home←{0=≢⍵:'/app/integrations/kafka' ⋄ ⍵}2⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'DYALOG_KAFKA_HOME'
      {}#.⎕FIX'file://',home,'/apl/Kafka.apln'
      {}#.⎕FIX'file://',home,'/apl/Orders.apln'
      #.Kafka.Init
    ∇

    Brokers←{0=≢⍵:'apl-kafka:19092' ⋄ ⍵}2⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'KAFKA_BROKERS'

    ∇ s←Restore;c;msgs
    ⍝ The last published summary, or an empty state. Reads order-stats from the
    ⍝ start with a one-off group, so it sees every summary ever published.
      c←#.Kafka.Consumer Brokers('stats-restore-',⍕⎕AI[2]+1000×⎕AI[3])'order-stats'
      msgs←1000000 3000 1000 #.Kafka.Poll c
      :If 0=≢msgs
          s←#.Orders.Empty
          ⎕←'No previous summary: starting from zero.'
      :Else
          s←#.Orders.FromSummary(⊃⌽msgs).data
          ⎕←'Restored totals from the last summary (',(⍕+/s.orders),' orders so far).'
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ (s n)←{wait}Step(s c p);msgs;orders
    ⍝ One batch: poll, add to the totals, publish a summary, confirm progress.
    ⍝ wait: ms to wait for the first message (default 2000).
      :If 0=⎕NC'wait' ⋄ wait←2000 ⋄ :EndIf
      msgs←500 wait 500 #.Kafka.Poll c
      n←≢msgs
      :If n=0 ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf
      orders←(⊂⍬)~⍨msgs.data                     ⍝ skip anything that isn't JSON
      s←s #.Orders.Add orders
      p #.Kafka.Send'order-stats'(#.Orders.Summary s)'summary'
      {}#.Kafka.Flush p
      {}c.commit                                 ⍝ tell Kafka these orders are done
      ⎕←'' ⋄ ⎕←'Batch of ',(⍕n),' orders · ',(⍕+/s.orders),' in total'
      ⎕←#.Orders.Table s
    ∇

    ∇ RunUntilIdle;c;p;s;n
    ⍝ Process everything waiting, then stop.
      Load
      s←Restore
      c←#.Kafka.Consumer Brokers'apl-processor' 'orders'
      p←#.Kafka.Producer Brokers
      ⍝ The first poll waits longer: after joining its group, a consumer gets
      ⍝ its partitions only once Kafka has rebalanced the group, which can
      ⍝ take seconds (longer if a previous processor was stopped abruptly).
      (s n)←20000 Step s c p
      :While n>0
          (s n)←Step s c p
      :EndWhile
      ⎕←'' ⋄ ⎕←'No new orders. Totals: ',(⍕+/s.orders),' orders, revenue ',⍕+/s.revenue
    ∇

    ∇ Run;c;p;s;n
    ⍝ Live: keep processing as orders arrive (stop with Ctrl+C).
      ⎕PW←200
      Load
      s←Restore
      c←#.Kafka.Consumer Brokers'apl-processor' 'orders'
      p←#.Kafka.Producer Brokers
      ⎕←'Waiting for orders on the "orders" topic. Ctrl+C to stop.'
      :While 1
          (s n)←Step s c p
      :EndWhile
    ∇
:EndNamespace
